# The mission arrow in Liberty City's opening (docs/MISSION_VM.md, "The arrow").
# Boot as krishna_walk.probe does, with one more Enter for the city screen.
# Stand still while the opening's arrow points at `137 TARGET`, then walk up
# for 3 s. Each dump is 10 MB from 0, which holds the page tables, so
# gta8.py's Ram reads it. The dumps gave:
# - the run-time values the arrow needs: 0x1cc1dc (78), the sine table at
#   0x1934a4, the tangent table behind [0x132524] and the draw flag 0x186ebc;
# - at each dump, the player, the view rectangle, the arrow's target, its
#   easing and the arrow object, which gfa_fixed::dos_trig's and the VM's
#   tests check against.
3500 tap esc 80
+2000 tap enter 80
+3000 tap enter 80
+1500 tap enter 80
+2000 tap enter 80
21000 shot start
22200 memdump a00 0 a00000
22201 shot f00
22300 memdump a01 0 a00000
22301 shot f01
22500 memdump a02 0 a00000
22501 shot f02
24000 memdump a03 0 a00000
24001 shot f03
27000 memdump a04 0 a00000
27001 shot f04
27100 down up
30100 up up
30200 memdump a05 0 a00000
30201 shot f05
30300 memdump a06 0 a00000
30301 shot f06
31000 quit
